{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Samuel judged Israel [C]all the days of his [Dm]life
Year af[Bb]ter year [C]he traveled the circuit [F]wide
Bet[Bb]hel, Gilgal, and Mizpah were [F]the places he [Dm]knew
Judging the people [C]in every place he [Dm]drew
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He returned to Ramah where his [C]home was [F]found
There he [Dm]judged Israel on the [C]sacred [F]ground
And he built an [Bb]altar to the LORD [Dm]there
Keeping the [Bb]promise [C]with unceasing [Dm]care
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
From the high places [C]down to the valley [Dm]floor
